\fs32 \cf2 In a compile-time context, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 IntLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 FloatLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values support all arithmetic operators except exponentiation (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 **
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ), and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 IntLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values support all bitwise and shift operators. In a run-time context, materialized 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 IntLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values are 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Int
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values and therefore support the same operators as 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Int
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and materialized 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 FloatLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values are 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values and therefore support the same operators as 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Comparison operators\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo supports a standard set of comparison operators: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ==
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 !=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 <
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 <=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 >
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 >=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . However their behavior depends on the type of values being compared.\
The remainder of this section describes numerical comparison operators. String comparisons are discussed in the \cf5 \ul \ulc5 String operators\cf2 \ulnone . Several other types in the Mojo standard library support various comparison operators, in particular the "equal" and "not equal" comparisons. Consult the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/lib/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul API documentation}} for a type to determine whether any comparison operators are supported.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

