\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ) with multi-element 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SIMD
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values return a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Bool
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  result using reduction semantics. The comparison is 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  only if it's true for all corresponding elements. For example:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf16 \cb15 simd8 \cf5 =\cf16  SIMD\cf5 [\cf16 DType\cf5 .\cf16 int32\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 4\cf5 ](\cf14 1\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 2\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 3\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 2\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf16 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
simd9 \cf5 =\cf16  SIMD\cf5 [\cf16 DType\cf5 .\cf16 int32\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 4\cf5 ](\cf14 1\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 2\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 4\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 2\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf5 \cb15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
print(\cf21 "simd8 == simd9:"\cf5 ,\cf16  simd8 \cf5 ==\cf16  simd9\cf5 )\cf16   \cf6 # False (element 2 differs)\cf16 \cb1 \
