\fs40 \cf2 String replication\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 *
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator replicates a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  a specified number of times. For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 var\cf16  str1\cf5 :\cf16  String \cf5 =\cf16  \cf21 "la"\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15 str2 \cf5 =\cf16  str1 \cf5 *\cf16  \cf14 5\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf16 str2\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf16 \cb15 lalalalala\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \cb12 StringLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  supports the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 *
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator for both compile-time and run-time string replication. The following examples perform compile-time string replication resulting in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 StringLiteral
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 comptime\cf16  divider1 \cf5 =\cf16  \cf21 "="\cf16  \cf5 *\cf16  \cf14 40\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 comptime\cf16  symbol \cf5 =\cf16  \cf21 "#"\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 comptime\cf16  divider2 \cf5 =\cf16  symbol \cf5 *\cf16  \cf14 40\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf16  \cf22 generate_divider\cf5 (\cf16 char\cf5 :\cf16  String\cf5 ,\cf16  repeat\cf5 :\cf16  Int\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 ->\cf16  String\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf16  char \cf5 *\cf16  repeat\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 comptime\cf16  divider3 \cf5 =\cf16  generate_divider\cf5 (\cf21 "~"\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf14 40\cf5 )\cf16   \cf6 # Evaluated at compile-time\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf16 divider1\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf16 divider2\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf16 divider3\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf16 \cb15 ========================================\cb1 \
\cb15 ########################################\cb1 \
\cb15 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 In contrast, the following examples perform run-time string replication resulting in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 String
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf16 \cb15 repeat \cf5 =\cf16  \cf14 40\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15 div1 \cf5 =\cf16  \cf21 "^"\cf16  \cf5 *\cf16  repeat\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf16 div1\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 print(\cf21 "_"\cf16  \cf5 *\cf16  repeat\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

