\fs64 \cf2 Implement operators for custom types\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 When you create a custom struct, Mojo allows you to define the behavior of many of the built-in operators for that type by implementing special dunder (double underscore) methods. This section lists the dunder methods associated with the operators and briefly describes the requirements for implementing them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb19 Currently, Mojo doesn't support defining arbitrary custom operators (for example, 
\fs24\fsmilli12250 \cf10 \cb20 -^-
\fs28 \cf2 \cb19 ). You can define behaviors for only the operators listed in the following subsections.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

