\fs40 \cf2 Implement overloaded arithmetic operators for 
\fs35 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1  values\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Our initial set of binary arithmetic operators work fine if both operands are 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  instances. But if we have a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  value representing just a real value, we'd first need to use it to create a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  value before we could add, subtract, multiply, or divide it with another 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  value. If we think that this will be a common use case, it makes sense to overload our arithmetic methods to accept a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  as the second operand.\
For the case where we have 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 complex1 + float1
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , we can just create an overloaded definition of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __add__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . But what about the case of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 float1 + complex1
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ? By default, when Mojo encounters a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 +
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator it tries to invoke the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __add__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method of the left-hand operand, but the built-in 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type doesn't implement support for addition with a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  value. This is an example where we need to implement the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __radd__()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method on the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  type. When Mojo can't find an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __add__(self, rhs: Complex) -> Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method defined on 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , it uses the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 __radd__(self, lhs: Float64) -> Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method defined on 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
So we can support arithmetic operations on 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  values by implementing the following eight methods.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf16 \cb15     \cf6 # ...\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __add__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 +\cf16  rhs\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __radd__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 +\cf16  lhs\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __sub__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 -\cf16  rhs\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __rsub__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 lhs \cf5 -\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 re\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf5 -\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __mul__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 *\cf16  rhs\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im \cf5 *\cf16  rhs\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __rmul__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 lhs \cf5 *\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 re\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs \cf5 *\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __truediv__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 /\cf16  rhs\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im \cf5 /\cf16  rhs\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __rtruediv__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cf5 )\cf16  raises \cf5 ->\cf16  Self\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         denom \cf5 =\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 squared_norm\cf5 ()\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  Self\cf5 (\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 (\cf16 lhs \cf5 *\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 re\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 /\cf16  denom\cf5 ,\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 (-\cf16 lhs \cf5 *\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 /\cf16  denom\cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
