\fs40 \cf2 Implement in-place assignment operators\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Now let's implement support for the in-place assignment operators: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 +=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 -=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 *=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 /=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . These modify the original value, so we need to mark 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 self
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  as being an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 mut
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  argument and update the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 re
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 im
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  fields instead of returning a new 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  instance. And once again, we'll overload the definitions to support both a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Complex
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operand.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf16 \cb15     \cf6 # ...\cf16 \cb1 \
