\fs48 \cf2 Implement equality operators\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The field of complex numbers is not an ordered field, so it doesn't make sense for us to implement the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Comparable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait and the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 >
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 >=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 <
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 <=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operators. However, we can implement the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Equatable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait and the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ==
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 !=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operators. (Of course, this suffers the same limitation of comparing floating point numbers for equality because of the limited precision of representing floating point numbers when performing arithmetic operations. But we'll go ahead and implement the operators for completeness.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 struct\cf16  \cf22 Complex\cf5 (\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     Equatable\cf5 ,\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf6 # ...\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __eq__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  other\cf5 :\cf16  Self\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 ->\cf16  Bool\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 ==\cf16  other\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 and\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im \cf5 ==\cf16  other\cf5 .\cf16 im\cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf22 __ne__\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  other\cf5 :\cf16  Self\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 ->\cf16  Bool\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 return\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 !=\cf16  other\cf5 .\cf16 re \cf5 or\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 im \cf5 !=\cf16  other\cf5 .\cf16 im\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

